# Line roles
{.lead} The {.lead} standfirst you are reading is one line role; a {.cite} attribution under a quote is the other.

> "Roles add intent to a line without adding style."
> {.cite} The spec, principle two

## Degradation (not tagged)
{.note} A standalone {.note} line role is not in the implemented set, so the engine strips the tag and renders this as a plain paragraph rather than failing. Shown only to document that fallback.
